{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792483003782,"sessionID":"ses_ea7b20775ffer3m9OaZg9u7076","part":{"id":"prt_158500d7d001zsj2zSmtNrwTm8","messageID":"msg_1584fc5e1001Myzv0QlLzGx08I","sessionID":"ses_ea7b20775ffer3m9OaZg9u7076","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1792483009704,"sessionID":"ses_ea7b20775ffer3m9OaZg9u7076","part":{"id":"prt_158500d80001kpFo45qVMLk1L5","messageID":"msg_1584fc5e1001Myzv0QlLzGx08I","sessionID":"ses_ea7b20775ffer3m9OaZg9u7076","type":"text","text":"The complete Zephyr RTOS application has been written to `submission/main.c`. \n\nThe application implements:\n\n1. **DMA controller acquisition** - Gets `dma0` from devicetree and checks readiness\n2. **Ping-pong buffers** - Two 32-byte buffers (`buf_a` and `buf_b`) for alternating DMA targets\n3. **Active buffer tracking** - Maintains which buffer is currently being filled by DMA\n4. **Circular/continuous mode** - The DMA callback automatically reloads and restarts the DMA transfer to the next buffer after each completion\n5. **Buffer reload mechanism** - On completion, switches active buffer and reconfigures DMA\n6. **Thread signaling** - Uses a semaphore to wake the main thread after each transfer\n7. **Transfer processing** - Main loop processes at least 4 completed transfers, printing buffer contents\n8. **DMA cleanup** - Stops the DMA channel after processing\n9. **Transfer counting** - Tracks and prints total number of completed transfers\n\nThe circular operation is achieved by the callback reconfiguring and restarting the DMA channel immediately upon each completion, creating continuous ping-pong buffering without gaps.","time":{"start":1792483003776,"end":1792483009698}}}
